WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions of "ATP Synthesis" by Drew Berry, wehi.tv, for HHMI BioInteractive, from the film's page on YouTube (youtu.be/CSrtewCJbpg).
Each cue is one line here, and mishearings in the captions are put right (plans/follow-the-molecule/captions.py lists them).

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.640
All life on Earth depends on this tiny energetic molecule,

2
00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:10.050
adenosine triphosphate or ATP.

3
00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:15.090
ATP drives biochemical activity inside your living cells

4
00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:20.100
and is a key building block of DNA and RNA.

5
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:23.140
Generating ATP for your living cells

6
00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.550
are mitochondria, electrochemical batteries

7
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:29.490
that convert energy from the food you eat

8
00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:34.240
and oxygen from the air you breathe into ATP.

9
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.480
So where does your ATP come from?

10
00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.800
Deep inside your mitochondria, rows of molecular motors

11
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:49.280
generate ATP, the molecule essential to all life on Earth.

12
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.850
Enzymes bring together reactants to form a chemical bond,

13
00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:00.130
converting mechanical energy into chemical energy.

14
00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:09.150
A ring of enzymes work in step, creating three molecules of ATP

15
00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.140
with each cycle.

16
00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:20.360
Inside the molecular motor, a rotating axle

17
00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.740
powers the sequence.

18
00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:28.380
The axle is attached to a rotary molecular motor moved

19
00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:31.777
by the force of protons pushing from the other side

20
00:01:31.777 --> 00:01:32.444
of the membrane.

21
00:01:35.692 --> 00:01:38.650
A difference in proton concentration

22
00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:48.705
propels the molecular mechanisms, synthesis of ATP.

23
00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:58.640
ATP drives biochemical activity inside your living cells

24
00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:03.490
and is a key building block of DNA and RNA.
